<title>USA: Lancer says sets three-for-two stock split.</title>
<headline>Lancer says sets three-for-two stock split.</headline>
<dateline>SAN ANTONIO, Texas 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lancer Corp said Tuesday its board of directors had approved a three-for-two split of the company's common stock to take the form of a 50 percent dividend payable July 8, 1997 to shareholders of record on June 24, 1997.</p>
<p>Lancer, which currently has 5,843,776 shares of common stock outstanding, said it was the third time in three years it had declared a three-for-two stock split.</p>
<p>Company chief executive officer George Schroeder said the stock price had again reached a level where a split would make the stock more attractively priced to new investors.</p>
<p>(( New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
